       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4,250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the usual maximum metformin dose. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, and the usual maximum is 2,000 mg/day. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis is serious, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **425 mg** three times daily. This isn't a standard tablet strength, so it's probably not the intended dose.\n- **850 mg** three times daily, which is 2,550 mg/day and the maximum labeled dose.\n- **500 mg** three times daily, or **1,000 mg** twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away: oral, three times daily with meals. If you really do intend 4,250 mg, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy or your attending first."
      }
