     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about 5 times the maximum labeled dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. Normal renal and hepatic function doesn't lower that risk enough.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that now, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower dose if you're titrating.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending.** If you think this dose is intended, for example because of a transcription error or a plan I don't know about, they can review it. If it's still ordered, it will need to go through their direct verification process.\n- **Check the source.** If the number came from a handoff, a note, or a calculation, it may have been mistranscribed.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
